>> servings: 2
>> source: https://www.jamieoliver.com/recipes/fish/punchy-salmon-salad/

Peel and finely slice 2 cloves of @garlic{2%cloves} and ½ a fresh @red chilli{1/2} (deseed if you like), then peel and finely grate a 2cm piece of @ginger{2%cm}. Pick the leaves from ½ a bunch of @coriander{1/2%bunch} (15g) and finely slice the stalks.

Scrape the skin of 1/4 of a @cucumber{1/4} with a fork to create grooves, halve it lengthways, then scoop out and discard the seeds. Finely slice into half moons, then place in a bowl and squeeze over the juice of 1 @lime{1}. Drizzle over 1 tablespoon of @sesame oil{1%tbsp} and toss together.

Put 300g of @new potatoes{300%g} into a #pan{}, cutting any larger potatoes in half, then cook in boiling salted water for 12 to ~{15%minutes}, or until tender.

Trim and roughly chop 160g of @green beans{160%g}, adding them to the pan for the last ~{4%minutes}. Drain and leave to steam dry.

Meanwhile, cut open 1 @green tea bag{1} (if using) and sprinkle the tea onto a plate. Add a good pinch of sea salt and black pepper, then roll the @salmon{225%g} in the mixture until completely covered.

Place a #non-stick frying pan{} over a medium heat, scatter in 1 tablespoon of @sesame seeds{1%tbsp} and toast until golden, then remove to a bowl.

Place the pan back on the heat, drizzle in 1 tablespoon of @groundnut oil{1%tbsp}, then add 1 x 225g @salmon fillet{1}, skin-side down. Fry for around ~{6%minutes}, or until the skin is golden and crisp. Flip over and cook for roughly 5 more minutes, or until just cooked through in the middle – this will vary slightly depending on the thickness of your salmon, so use your instincts. Remove the salmon to a board, skin-side up, and leave to cool a little.

Pop the frying pan back on a medium heat. Drizzle in 1 tablespoon of groundnut oil, add the garlic, chilli, ginger and coriander stalks, then fry for a couple of minutes, or until lightly golden.

Add the cooked veg, and using a #potato masher{}, lightly crush the potatoes. Toss everything together, season to taste with sea salt and black pepper, then fry for a couple of minutes. Remove from the heat.

Trim and finely slice 2 @spring onions{2}, stir them through the potatoes with the coriander leaves, then spoon onto a serving platter.

Flake over the cooked salmon and sprinkle with the toasted sesame seeds. Serve with the pickled cucumber and cut the remaining @lime{1} wedges for squeezing over.
